/** Records the cancelled statement, once it is removed. */
=== statement/AuditStatement.java
/** Records the statement, once it is saved; the date it was taken as of last, when one was given. */
=== statement/BindingLog.java
/** One binding of a person's claims, with the sheet's today when it was made: a statement's (each claim it bound,
 *  with its figure) or a cancel's (none bound). */
=== statement/CancelStatement.java
/**
 * Cancels the person's last statement: it is removed, and the claims it bound are live again (a figure bound by a
 * statement before it is not restored). Only a steward cancels, and a person with no statement has none to cancel.
 * Returns the cancelled statement, for the audit.
 */
=== statement/Statement.java
/** A statement taken for a person: their due-total then (two decimals, or n/a), the date it was taken as of (the
 *  sheet's today then when none was given) and the sheet's today when it was taken. */
=== statement/TakeStatement.java
/**
 * Takes a statement for the person: records their due-total now, on the sheet's today, and binds each of
 * their claims that counts to the figure it has now (never its late charge, which keeps following the sheet's today); their claims that do not count (a person's unbound OPEN ones dated within a
 * hold among them) are unbound (live again).
 * <p>
 * Taken as of a date (on or before the sheet's today, and not before the person was added), it works the same out
 * as at the end of that date: every change made while the sheet's today was on or before it counts (a claim's status
 * and settled due, the rates, settings, grades, holds, retirement and the claims bound), every later change does not,
 * and that date stands in for the sheet's today. The claims that counted then are bound to their figures then; every
 * other claim of theirs is unbound.
 */
=== period/ApplyPeriod.java
/** Adds the period to the sheet; refuses a name the sheet already has and dates overlapping another period's. */
=== period/AuditPeriodAdded.java
/** Records the period, once it is added. */
=== period/AuditPeriodClosed.java
/** Records the period's closing, with the due-total it fixed. */
=== period/AuditPeriodReopened.java
/** Records the period's reopening. */
=== period/AuditPeriodsGenerated.java
/** Records each period a generate made, in month order, as an added period. */
=== period/AuditPeriodSoftClosed.java
/** Records the period's soft close, with the due-total it fixed. */
=== period/AutoClosePeriods.java
/** Once the sheet's today is changed, with grace days set, closes each open period (not a soft-closed one, whose totals stay as fixed) whose to-date plus the grace
 *  days is before the new today, in order of their to-dates, fixing its totals exactly as a close by hand would (the
 *  permission matrix governs closing by hand, not this), recording each closing with auto=yes, and keeping it in the sheet's history as of its to-date (its end). */
=== period/ClosePeriod.java
/** Closes the period, fixing each person's due-total for it as it is now — the dues (with any late charge, as shown now) of the claims whose due-by falls in it that counted by the status they had at the end of its last day (not a person's
 *  unbound OPEN ones dated within a hold of theirs), added up, skipping n/a, 0.00 for one with none — and its own, their sum. A soft-closed period can be closed, fixing them afresh. Refuses a period already closed, and a close by a role the sheet's permission matrix does not
 *  allow to (by the standing rule, clerk and steward may). */
=== period/GeneratedPeriods.java
/** The periods a generate made, in month order. */
=== period/GeneratePeriods.java
/** Adds a period per calendar month from the from-date's month to the to-date's, each from the first to the last
 *  day of its month and named yyyy-mm, leaving out a month whose name the sheet already has or whose days overlap
 *  a period; refuses a date that is not a calendar date and a to-date before the from-date. */
=== period/GeneratePeriodsRequest.java
/** The generate-periods form as submitted: a from and a to date (YYYY-MM-DD), either blank for the sheet's today. */
=== period/InvalidPeriodException.java
/** A period that cannot be added: no name, a date that is not a calendar date, a to-date before its
 *  from-date, a name the sheet already has, or dates overlapping another period's; or one that cannot be
 *  closed (already closed) or reopened (not closed, or not by a steward). */
=== period/LoadPeriod.java
/** Loads a period of the sheet by id. */
=== period/PeriodInput.java
/** A validated period form: the trimmed name, and its from and to date, from on or before to. */
=== period/Period.java
/** A sheet's period: a name (unique on the sheet) and a from and to date, inclusive; once closed, its due-total
 *  and each person's are fixed at what they were on closing, until a steward reopens it. */
=== period/PeriodNotFoundException.java
/** No period with that id on the sheet. */
=== period/PeriodRequest.java
/** The period form as submitted: a name, and its from and to date (YYYY-MM-DD). */
=== period/PeriodResponse.java
/** A period as the screen shows it: its name, its from and to date (YYYY-MM-DD), whether it is closed, whether it is soft-closed, and the
 *  due-total fixed when it was closed (null while open), and each person's fixed then, by person id (empty while open). */
=== period/ReopenPeriod.java
/** Reopens a closed or soft-closed period, so its due-total is live again. Only a role the sheet's permission matrix allows to
 *  reopen may (a steward, by the standing rule); refuses a period
 *  that is not closed. */
=== period/RespondWithPeriods.java
/** The sheet's periods; as of a date (asOf), as they stood at the end of it. */
=== period/SoftClosePeriod.java
/** Soft-closes the period, fixing each person's due-total for it and its own exactly as closing does, while claims
 *  whose due-by falls in it can still be added, edited and change status. Refuses a period already closed or soft-closed, and a
 *  soft close by a role the sheet's permission matrix does not allow to close. */
=== period/ValidateGeneratePeriods.java
/** Reads the generate-periods form from the body; its dates are checked once the sheet (and its today) is loaded. */
=== period/ValidatePeriod.java
/** Reads the period form from the body, trimming the name; refuses an empty name, a from- or to-date that is
 *  not a calendar date, and a to-date before the from-date. */
=== rate/ApplyRate.java
/** Sets the grade's rate from the from-date on the sheet, replacing the one it had for that from-date, and logs it
 *  with the sheet's today (so the rates can be worked out as they stood on an earlier date). */
=== rate/AuditRateSet.java
/** Records the grade's rate, once it is saved. */
=== rate/InvalidRateException.java
/** A rate form that cannot be saved: a grade other than A, B or C, or a percent that is missing, negative or has more than two decimals,
 *  or a to-date before its from-date. */
=== rate/RateInput.java
/** A validated rate form: the grade, its percent with two decimals and its from-date and to-date (null when none). */
=== rate/Rate.java
/** A sheet's rate for a grade: a percent with two decimals, from a date on (null: from the beginning of time),
 *  through a to-date (null: no end). */
=== rate/RateLog.java
/** One rate set on a sheet, as it was set, with the sheet's today then. */
=== rate/RatePreviewInput.java
/** A validated rate preview: the grade and the candidate percent with two decimals. */
=== rate/RatePreviewResponse.java
/** A rate preview: how many claims would show a different due, and the sum of the differences ("3.00", "-1.50"). */
=== rate/RateRequest.java
/** The rate form as submitted: a grade, its percent and its from-date (blank: from the beginning of time)
 *  and its to-date (blank: no end). */
=== rate/RateResponse.java
/** A grade's rate as the screen shows it: the percent with two decimals and its from-date and to-date (null when none). */
=== rate/RespondWithRatePreview.java
/** What a candidate rate would do: of the OPEN and PENDING claims whose person had the grade on the claim's date,
 *  not bound by a statement, how many would show a different due were the candidate the grade's rate on every date,
 *  and the sum of the differences (new due minus current due; n/a counts as 0.00). Nothing is saved. */
=== rate/RespondWithRates.java
/** The sheet's rates; as of a date (asOf), as they stood at the end of it. */
=== rate/ValidateRate.java
/** Reads the rate form from the body; refuses a grade other than A, B or C and a percent that is missing, negative or has more than two decimals,
 * a from-date or to-date that is not a calendar date, and a to-date before the from-date. A blank from-date means from the beginning of time. */
=== rate/ValidateRatePreview.java
/** Reads the rate preview from the query; refuses a grade other than A, B or C and a candidate percent that is
 *  missing, negative or has more than two decimals. */
=== holiday/ApplyHoliday.java
/** Adds the holiday to the sheet; refuses a date already on its list. Every claim on the sheet that is not SETTLED or
 * VOID and whose due-by is on or after the new holiday has its due-by worked out again, from the date and with the
 * terms it was fixed with, over the holidays now on the sheet; every other claim keeps its due-by. */
=== holiday/AuditHolidayAdded.java
/** Records the holiday, once it is added. */
=== holiday/BusinessDays.java
/** Business days: every day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or one of the sheet's holidays. */
=== holiday/Holiday.java
/** A sheet's holiday: a date, on the sheet at most once. */
=== holiday/HolidayRequest.java
/** The holiday entry as submitted: a date (YYYY-MM-DD). */
=== holiday/HolidayResponse.java
/** A holiday as the screen shows it: its date (YYYY-MM-DD). */
=== holiday/InvalidHolidayException.java
/** A holiday that cannot be added: a date that is not a calendar date, or one already on the sheet's list. */
=== holiday/RespondWithHolidays.java
/** The sheet's holidays, by date. */
=== holiday/ValidateHoliday.java
/** Reads the holiday's date from the body; refuses one that is not a calendar date. */
=== paste/AddPastedClaims.java
/**
 * Finds each line's person on the sheet, ignoring case, and makes its DRAFT claim by the claim form's rules —
 * all of them before any is stored, so a refused line adds nothing; a line repeating a reference of an earlier
 * line, ignoring case, is refused too. Then adds the claims in order, each recorded
 * and logged as the claim form records and logs it.
 */
=== paste/PastedClaims.java
/** How many claims the paste added. */
=== paste/PastedLine.java
/** One pasted line once checked by the claim form's rules: the trimmed name and the claim it makes. */
=== paste/PastedLines.java
/** Every line of the paste box, in order. */
=== paste/PasteRequest.java
/** The paste box as submitted: lines of name,amount,date,note. */
=== paste/ValidatePaste.java
/**
 * Reads the paste box from the body: each non-blank line is name,amount,date,note — the note is the rest of the
 * line, so it may hold commas; the date and the note may be blank or absent. A trimmed note ending in
 * " #<reference>" gives the claim that reference, and the note is what comes before it. Checks every line's claim exactly
 * as the claim form would (it corrects nothing), refusing the whole paste when any line fails or there is none.
 */
=== quickadd/CheckQuickAddDate.java
/** Refuses the quick-add before anyone is added when its claim, dated the sheet's entry date (else its today), would have
 *  its due-by in a closed period: the date plus the named person's terms (a person not on the sheet yet is added with
 *  grade A and no terms of their own) — so a refused claim leaves no new person behind. */
=== quickadd/FindOrAddPerson.java
/**
 * Finds the named person on the sheet, ignoring case; when there is none, adds them with grade A and records
 * it as the person form would (the person, then how the figures moved), noting the figures afterwards so the
 * claim's own rollup counts only what the claim moved.
 */
=== quickadd/QuickAddName.java
/** The trimmed name the quick-add bar was given. */
=== quickadd/QuickAddRequest.java
/** The quick-add bar as submitted: the name of the person and the amount of their new draft claim. */
=== quickadd/ValidateQuickAdd.java
/**
 * Reads the quick-add bar from the body, trimming the name; refuses an empty name, and an amount the claim
 * form would refuse. Publishes the claim as the claim form would: the sheet's today, with an empty note.
 */
=== watch/ApplyWatch.java
/** Starts or stops the signed-in user watching the person; says whether that changed anything (watching one
 *  already watched, or stopping one not watched, changes nothing). */
=== watch/AuditWatch.java
/** Records the user starting or stopping watching the person, once it is saved, when it changed anything. */
=== watch/NotifyWatchers.java
/** After the claim's own line: when the claim has just been settled (settled, approved or re-settled), one line
 *  for each user watching its person, in the order they started watching. */
=== watch/RespondWithWatched.java
/** The ids of the people on the sheet the user watches; as of a date (asOf), as they stood at the end of it. */
=== watch/ValidateWatch.java
/** Reads whether to start (true) or stop (false) watching; refuses a body without it, or no signed-in name. */
=== watch/WatchChange.java
/** Whether a watch request changed what the user watches. */
=== watch/WatchInput.java
/** A validated watch request: whether the signed-in user starts (true) or stops (false) watching. */
=== watch/Watch.java
/** A signed-in name watching a person: told of each of their claims settled, approved or re-settled. */
=== history/AsOf.java
/**
 * A sheet as it stood at the end of a date (an as-of view): every change made while the sheet's today was on or
 * before it counts, every later one does not, and that date stands in for the sheet's today. With no date, each
 * read gives the sheet as the store holds it now. Only worked out, never saved.
 */
=== history/History.java
/**
 * The states a sheet's things have been saved in (entity_history), each with the sheet's today when it was saved —
 * recorded by HistoryRecorder — and read back as they stood at the end of a date: the last state saved while the
 * sheet's today was on or before it. A thing with no state saved by then did not exist then (or was deleted); one
 * with no state recorded at all was saved before this was kept and stands as it is.
 */
=== history/HistoryRecorder.java
/**
 * Records into entity_history the state each kept entity (see History) is in once a change to it is saved: as the
 * transaction completes, one state per entity it inserted, updated (its fields or its collections) or deleted (no
 * state), each with its sheet's today then.
 */

